@startuml bff-design
!include _style.puml
title Playground web server (BFF): ports and adapters (built; planned parts in white)
' palette: edge=blue · use case=green · domain=amber · port=lavender · adapter=lavender · infrastructure=gray
' Shows the web server of apps/web/src as built (decision 5): the Next.js edge, the use cases, the pure domain,
' the four ports and their adapters, and composition.ts, the only place that picks adapters.
' PLANNED, NOT BUILT (decision 12), drawn as white boxes with a "planned" stereotype:
'   - a new session ends this browser's earlier session
'   - a use case that decides what a session may see (active, pending, deactivated, signed out) and ends both
'     sessions for a deactivated person by reusing sign out
'   - attempts looked up by state, so a refused older callback does not use up the newer attempt
'   - a security log port (NFR-5)
' WARNING: the IdentityProvider port here (sign in, refresh, end session) is a DIFFERENT port with the same
' name as the API's IdentityProvider in access-design.puml (which enables and disables people in Keycloak).
' Not drawn: pages and components (thin, no ports of their own), lib/utils.ts, the Keycloak login page.

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype polyline
top to bottom direction

class "proxy.ts\ncookie gate" as PRX #E6F0FB
class "Routes\nlogin, callback,\nlogout, backend" as RT #E6F0FB
class "lib/auth, lib/api\ncookies, getMe" as LIB #E6F0FB
class "composition.ts\nonly place that\npicks adapters,\nbuilds SignIn\nand SignOut" as COMP #ECECEC

class "«use case»\nSignIn" as SI #E7F4EA {
  +startLogin()
  +finishLogin()
}
class "«use case»\nSignOut" as SO #E7F4EA {
  +signOut()
}
class "«use case»\nAccessToken" as AT #E7F4EA {
  +accessTokenFor()
  one refresh at a time
}
class "«use case»\nCallBackend" as CB #E7F4EA {
  +callBackend()
}
class "«planned»\nSessionVisibility" as SV #FFFFFF {
  +decide(status)
}

class "«rule»\nsafeReturnTo" as SR #FFE6CC
class "«value object»\nLoginAttempt" as LA #FFE6CC {
  state, nonce, pkceVerifier
  returnTo, startedAt
  +isExpired()
}
class "«value object»\nSession" as SE #FFE6CC {
  idToken, accessToken
  refreshToken, accessExpiresAt
  +needsRefresh()
}

class "«port»\nIdentityProvider" as PIDP #EEE7F7 {
  +endSessionUrl()
}
class "«port»\nLoginAttemptStore" as PLAS #EEE7F7 {
  +save()
  +take(id)
  «planned» +takeByState()
}
class "«port»\nSessionStore" as PSS #EEE7F7 {
  +take(id)
}
class "«port»\nBackendApi" as PBA #EEE7F7
class "«planned»\nSecurityLog" as PLOG #FFFFFF {
  +record(event)
}

class "«adapter»\nKeycloakIdentity-\nProvider" as KIDP #EEE7F7
class "«adapter»\nInMemoryLogin-\nAttemptStore" as MLAS #EEE7F7
class "«adapter»\nInMemory-\nSessionStore" as MSS #EEE7F7
class "«adapter»\nFetchBackendApi" as FBA #EEE7F7
class "«planned»\nConsoleSecurity-\nLog" as CLOG #FFFFFF

class "Keycloak" as KC #ECECEC
class "Playground API" as API #ECECEC

RT --> COMP
LIB --> COMP
PRX -[hidden]right- RT
RT -[hidden]right- LIB
COMP ..> SI : builds
COMP -[hidden]down- SI

SI -[hidden]right- SO
SO -[hidden]right- AT
SI -[hidden]down- CB
CB -[hidden]right- SV
SI --> SR
SI --> LA
AT --> SE
CB --> AT
SV ..> SO : reuses
SR -[hidden]down- SE
SI -[hidden]right- SR
SV -[hidden]right- LA

SI --> PLAS
SI --> PIDP
SI --> PSS
AT --> PSS
SO --> PSS
SO --> PIDP
AT --> PIDP
CB --> PBA
SV ..> PLOG

PIDP -[hidden]right- PLAS
PLAS -[hidden]right- PSS
PIDP -[hidden]down- PBA
PBA -[hidden]right- PLOG
PIDP <|.. KIDP
PLAS <|.. MLAS
PSS <|.. MSS
PBA <|.. FBA
PLOG <|.. CLOG
KIDP -[hidden]right- MLAS
MLAS -[hidden]right- MSS
KIDP -[hidden]down- FBA
FBA -[hidden]right- CLOG
KIDP ..> KC : ACL
FBA ..> API : bearer token
KC -[hidden]right- API

note as N
  Layers, top to bottom: Next.js edge,
  use cases and domain, ports, adapters,
  outside systems. proxy.ts only checks
  that a session cookie exists.
  PLANNED, not built (decision 12), white:
  - finishLogin takes the attempt by
    state, compares it, then exchanges
    the code
  - a new session ends this browser's
    earlier one
  - SignIn, SignOut and SessionVisibility
    write to SecurityLog
end note
CLOG -[hidden]right- N
@enduml
